@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Public Analyze — saved grammar, immutable tests and separate verdicts
start
:Prepare public browser session;\nload the saved shared grammar;
:Type text or copy a reference unchanged;\nshow public-retention/privacy notice;
:Submit request_id, exact text and saved grammar;
:Check allowlist, Origin, CSRF,\nrequest limits and payload;
if (Request permitted?) then (yes)
  :Bind PublicWorkspaceStore;\nacquire course_operation shared lock;
else (no)
  :Show the explicit HTTP error;\nno analysis is dispatched;
  stop
endif
if (Grammar is current or request_id already exists?) then (yes)
  :Look up prior test for the stable public actor\nand this request_id;
else (no)
  :Return 409; reload saved grammar;\nkeep the user's typed text;
  stop
endif
if (Prior request exists?) then (yes)
  if (Exact text and grammar_source match?) then (yes)
    :Reuse the original immutable snapshot;\ndo not recompute or insert;
  else (no)
    :Return 409 request-ID conflict;\ndo not overwrite the earlier result;
    stop
  endif
else (no)
  :Analyze CFG notation and transformations;
  if (Grammar can be analyzed within bounds?) then (yes)
    :Load Collection; build reviewed-word lexicon;\ntokenize and classify exact input;
  else (no)
    :Return explicit validation error;\nno snapshot inserted;
    stop
  endif
  :Calculate lexical statistics and predictive trace;\nvalidate RecordedTest and exact-match metadata;
  :Authorize a new analyzer_test only;\ninsert snapshot + request mapping in one transaction;\nincrement shared version;
endif
:Derive vocabulary approval from UNKNOWN count;\nattach redacted ownership; release shared lock;
:Show vocabulary ACCEPT / REJECT and CFG result separately;\nrefresh saved-test report when requested;
stop
legend bottom
  Analyze in the UI records a public test; Collection is never mutated by this workflow.
  A missing CFG table cell, non-LL(1) grammar or parser bound can yield a retained rejected test.
  Stopping client-side waiting does not cancel or roll back a server commit; inspect saved tests before retry.
  An existing identical retry may return its old snapshot even after offline grammar curation.
endlegend
@enduml
